  "summary": "Held the entire episode. The long entry worked immediately and extended almost monotonically from +9.5 to a peak near +110.5 by t=32-36m, then gave back to a still-strongly-positive +64.5 by t=42m. There was no point where the entry looked wrong-direction: every pullback stayed well above breakeven and each dip was followed by fresh highs or stabilization, never a sustained push toward zero or negative. Next time I'd watch for a pullback that actually threatens to erase the bulk of realized gains (not just off a local peak) combined with persistent negative 1m/5m body plus falling ER10/hurst as the real wrong-direction tell, rather than reacting to normal giveback in a strong trend."
